  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This serves 4 and takes about 1 hour. The thing to watch is the egusi frying stage: the ground seeds need to cook in the hot palm oil for a full 10-15 minutes, stirring regularly, until they turn from pale and raw-smelling to golden and nutty. Undercooked egusi makes the soup grainy and bitter."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The smoked fish gives the soup its deep, savoury backbone. Do not substitute fresh fish here as you will lose the characteristic flavour that makes egusi soup what it is."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
